  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Ain't It A Sin**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **The World (Is Going Up In Flames)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Why Is It So Hard**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Drop Hop**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Bewildered**: rare: 11 archived performances [3]\n- **Torture**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Get Back**: rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **Them Changes**: back after 24 archived shows (727 days); rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2015-03-12.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac24** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 14 songs; 126 min [1]\n- **soulive2015-03-12.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac16**: matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 14 songs; 126 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Charles Bradley [1]\n- The show was night one of Bowlive VI at Brooklyn Bowl [1]\n- The show was night one of Bowlive VI at Brooklyn Bowl [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2015-03-12.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: On Stage Audience/SBD Matrix [1]. Also: Matrix of two sources: on-stage Schoeps cmc622xt mics through Sonosax, Apogee and Sound Devices 744T, plus soundboard feed, both at 24/96; Time-aligned in SoundForge Pro 11, mixed and rendered in Vegas Pro 13; this is the 24-bit version of the release [1]\n- **soulive2015-03-12.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: On Stage Audience/SBD Matrix [2]. Also: Matrix of on-stage Schoeps mics and Digidesign/Avid Profile soundboard feed, each recorded to a Sound Devices 744T at 24/96; Downconverted to 16-bit/44.1 using iZotope SRC and MBIT+ dither; recorded, mixed and mastered by Eric McRoberts [2]",
